    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6132" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călactē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καλὴ ἀκτή</span> (i. e. Fair Beach), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town on the north coast of
			Sicily</i>, now <i>Caronia</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 43, § 101</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sil.
				14, 251</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călactīnus</span></b> , i,
			m., <i>an inhabitant of Calacte</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 22, § 49</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id.
				Fam. 13, 37</span></i>.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Calactini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 43, § 101</span></i>
			.</div>
